{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline task #5252 on branch `task/generation-run44-5252`. The task is to implement srd021-tac R2.1 through R2.4 (separator options: -s, -b, -r) in the existing `cmd/tac/` package. Specifically:\n   - R2.1: `-s SEP` must use SEP as the record separator instead of newline. SEP may be any string.\n   - R2.2: By default the separator follows each record. `-b` must place the separator before each record instead of after it.\n   - R2.3: `-r` must interpret the `-s SEP` argument as a regular expression (Go regexp syntax). Each match becomes a record boundary.\n   - R2.4: When `-s` and `-r` are combined, the separator is a regex; records are the text between consecutive matches.\n   \n   The task explicitly states to EXTEND existing files (design decision D1: do not rewrite from scratch) and add new differential test cases to the existing TestDiff function (D2).\n\n   Acceptance criteria require: functionality in main.go (AC1), differential tests covering R2.1-R2.4 (AC2), successful `go build` (AC3), `go vet` passes (AC4), and `go test` passes or skips gracefully (AC5).\n\n   CRITICAL constraints: No git commands. No filesystem exploration. No reading files already in project_context. Git is managed externally by the orchestrator.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (gtac) comparison via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Record separator modes: after-record (default), before-record (`-b`), regex mode (`-r`)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct: `{Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize}`\n   - Reference binary looku